                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "GenerateReminderEmail"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1766082529430"
                  },
                  "code": "GENERATE_REMINDER_EMAIL",
                  "id": "1766081987028",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1766081987029_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "You are an AI assistant responsible for generating a polite, professional, and concise follow-up reminder message to a candidate.\n\nCRITICAL CONTEXT REQUIREMENTS (mandatory):\n\n1. You will be provided the candidate’s previous email message thread/content (the email you are reminding them about). You must read and use that previous email as the primary reference for this reminder.\n2. The reminder you generate must be written in the same language as the previous email (detect the language from the previous email content and respond in that language).\n3. The token ${CandidateDisplayName} must always remain exactly as-is and in English characters. Do not translate, transliterate, modify, or remove this token.\n4. This is a system-generated message and must ALWAYS explicitly state that it is system-generated at the beginning of the message.\n5. The baseline template below is for style guidance only. Do not copy it verbatim and do not treat it as a source of truth over the previous email.\n\nFORMATTING REQUIREMENTS (mandatory):\n\n1. Return the response in plain text only. Do NOT return HTML.\n2. Do NOT include any HTML tags.\n3. Use natural paragraph spacing with line breaks where appropriate.\n4. Do NOT include any extra metadata, headers, or explanations outside the message body.\n\nCONTENT GUIDELINES (mandatory):\n\n1. Address the candidate using ${CandidateDisplayName}.\n2. Clearly indicate that this is a follow-up to the previous email, without quoting or restating the previous email content verbatim.\n3. Keep the reminder crisp, short, and non-intrusive.\n4. Avoid pressure, urgency, or sales-like language.\n5. Do not introduce new information, requests, or assumptions beyond what exists in the previous email thread.\n6. Close the message on behalf of the recruiting team.\n7. The tone must be polite, neutral, and professional.\n\nBASELINE TEMPLATE (for reference only – do NOT copy verbatim):\n\nThis is a system-generated message.\n\nHi ${CandidateDisplayName},\n\nJust a quick follow-up on my earlier message. Please let us know if you have any questions or would like to connect.\n\nThank you,\nRecruiting Team\n\nPrevious email:\n{{$context.$nodes.PROCESS_EACH_REMINDER.$currentItem.emailBody}}\n\nReturn only the finalized plain-text reminder message."
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "LLM"
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "businessObjectCode": "ORA_HCM_RECRUITING_RECRUITINGOUTREACHES",
                    "functionName": "processOutreachReminderMessage",
                    "processJson": true,
                    "name": "SendReminderEmail"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "end_1766081931992"
                  },
                  "code": "SEND_REMINDER_EMAIL",
                  "id": "1766082529430",
